# ClimateTweetStats

This R package provides tools for analyzing public sentiment towards climate change using tweet-based data,
including temperature trends, geographic location, and emotional response over time.
**note: While this package does not implement S3 or S4 class methods, it leverages
modern R programming techniques including data manipulation, statistical modeling,
and flexible input handling using the dplyr, ggplot2, and stats libraries.**


To install the package from GitHub:

# install.packages("devtools")
devtools::install_github("cplbabycodes/ClimateTweetStats")
library(ClimateTweetStats)

Features
Cleaning & Summarizing
Trend Visualization
Comparing Analysis

